From: gokay-ai <60583610+gokay-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:31:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] [Bugfix][Spec Decode] Propagate rope hf_overrides to the
 MTP draft

Covers the --hf-overrides YaRN path: nested text_config.rope_parameters
and max_position_embeddings are forwarded to the draft ModelConfig and
applied before the arch mapping. Replaces our local patch; its
wrapper-mirror leg was already dead at this base. Upstream's own
compose_draft_hf_overrides forwards callables only, so without this the
MTP draft stays on native rope while the target runs YaRN and acceptance
collapses past the draft's native window (#58080).

Forwarding is restricted to the MTP family (method in MTPModelTypes):
fused heads carry no rope of their own and must inherit the target's
extension, while an independent draft model ships its own rope config
and target dicts must not resize it (upstream
test_independent_draft_model_keeps_its_own_limit pins that contract).

Fixed from the PR as merged here: the annotations said PretrainedConfig
(HF spelling), which this tree never imports; speculative.py raised
NameError at import. Renamed to PreTrainedConfig.

Upstream-PR: vllm-project/vllm#58094 (gokay-ai, pending)
